IMPORT prelude

-- Industrial Relations Act 1979 (WA) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), no
-- daydate. The Act counts "no later than 28 days after the day on which" (s 29(2)), "within 6 years after the day on
-- which" (s 82A), "more than 24 months after" (s 51BU), "within 14 days after" (ss 51BK, 51BV) and "not ... more than 6
-- years prior to" (s 83A(2)). The Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(b) excludes the day of the event from a period
-- reckoned after it, s 61(1)(e) moves a time limit that falls on a Saturday or Sunday to the next weekday (holidays are
-- not computed: fork F2 in NOTES.md), and s 62(3) reckons a period of months to the numerically corresponding date less
-- one, or the last day of the month where there is none (fork F3).
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 2026-09-07: "Industrial Relations Act 1979", State of
-- Western Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Industrial Relations Act 1979`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(e), (2): a time limit that falls on an excluded day runs to the next day that is
-- not one. Saturdays and Sundays only (the serial day number modulo 7 is 6 on a Saturday and 0 on a Sunday).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next day that is not a Saturday or Sunday from` `the day` MEANS
    IF (DATE_SERIAL `the day`) MODULO 7 EQUALS 6
    THEN DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS 2)
    ELSE IF (DATE_SERIAL `the day`) MODULO 7 EQUALS 0
         THEN DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS 1)
         ELSE `the day`

-- The last day of a period of N days after a day (s 61(1)(b)), moved past a Saturday or Sunday (s 61(1)(e)).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the time limit of` n `days after` `the start` MEANS `the next day that is not a Saturday or Sunday from` (`the day` n `days after` `the start`)

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0 AND (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0)))
    OR  y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0

-- The date numerically corresponding to a day and month in another year; 29 February in a year that has none is
-- taken as 1 March, so that "less one" lands on the last day of February (s 62(3)).
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the corresponding date` d m y MEANS
    IF d EQUALS 29 AND m EQUALS 2 AND (NOT (`is a leap year` y))
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 y
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- The last day of a period of N years (12 N months) after a day: the period begins the next day (s 61(1)(b)) and runs
-- to the numerically corresponding date less one (s 62(3)). Not moved for a weekend.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of` n `years after` `the event` MEANS
    `the day` (-1) `days after` (`the corresponding date` (DATE_DAY `the next day`) (DATE_MONTH `the next day`) (DATE_YEAR `the next day` PLUS n))
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS `the day` 1 `days after` `the event`

-- A time limit of N years after a day, moved past a Saturday or Sunday (s 61(1)(e)).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the time limit of` n `years after` `the event` MEANS `the next day that is not a Saturday or Sunday from` (`the last day of` n `years after` `the event`)

-- The earliest day of a period of N years ending the day before a day: the day numerically corresponding N years
-- earlier (29 February in a year that has none taken as 1 March, fork F3).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the later day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest day of` n `years before` `the later day` MEANS
    `the corresponding date` (DATE_DAY `the later day`) (DATE_MONTH `the later day`) (DATE_YEAR `the later day` MINUS n)

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is before` `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`
